WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.892
This visual shows the effect of changing grain.

00:00:02.892 --> 00:00:05.902
The source table has one row per order.

00:00:05.902 --> 00:00:10.642
After DATE_TRUNC and GROUP BY, the result has one row per month.

00:00:10.642 --> 00:00:13.417
The chart is not just a different display.

00:00:13.417 --> 00:00:16.332
It represents a different analytical grain.

00:00:16.332 --> 00:00:21.132
Always be clear about what one row means before and after aggregation.

00:00:21.132 --> 00:00:28.807
EXTRACT returns a component such as month number or year; DATE_TRUNC returns a timestamp aligned to a time

00:00:28.807 --> 00:00:33.272
boundary such as the start of the month.

00:00:33.272 --> 00:00:39.872
For grouping over multiple years, truncating to month is often safer than grouping by month number alone

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:43.880
because January 2025 and January 2026 should not be merged accidentally.
